{
  "doc": "M3-C04-02 greybox: ch04/brightwater_ferry (act1_ch04.md C4-09 to C4-15). North is -z. The islet's seaward landing (south: stone steps to deep water, the far side from the Shell Shrine door), the gangplank, the ferry Kind Weather (a two-masted Low Reaches coastal ferry: the deckhouse with its small Order shrine, the purser, the passengers' awning, cargo lashed amidships, the skiff on its davits, the wheel aft, the bow), and, west of her across an oar's length of open water, the drifting Seventh Terrace (the stern and its name-board, the galley with four bowls, the hold hatch, the mainmast with her set sails and the Spar-Wraith in the rigging). The two hulls are never joined: there is no walkway between them (ADR 0017 (d): the ferry is never attacked, and nothing from the derelict comes aboard her). Rails keep Rhen out of the sea, which is a solid floor 2 m down. The derelict's random fights (encounters) run only while the party is aboard her, between ch04_boarded_derelict and ch04_spar_wraith_defeated, so none can ever start on the ferry. states (Ch04Zone): the gangplank shipped once Ysolde has joined; the party across on the derelict from ch04_boarded_derelict; the sails down and the wraith gone from ch04_spar_wraith_defeated; the board off the stern and wrapped on the ferry's deck, and the party back aboard, from ch04_name_board_carried. Env-art's ferry and derelict kit (M3-C04-03) replaces the blocks.",
